    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "SAFETY INSTRUCTIONS\nDC-8\n30/50\nB*Ai E JAPAN AIR LINES\nJAL\nIN CASE OF EMERGENCY\nThis aircraft incorporates all safety features.\nIn case of an emergency, please remain calm\nand follow the instructions of the crew.\nKindly read the directions below.\nEVACUATION SLIDE\nEMERGENCY EVACUATION POSITIONS\nCOCKPIT\nFORWARD\nENTRANCE\nGALLEY\nLAVATORY\nPull off cover plate and\ndiscard\nPull down bars to the floor.\nFIRST\nCLASS\nCABIN\nEMERGENCY→\nEXITS\nTo inflate slide pull yellow tab.\nSit and slide down.\nTO OPEN EMERGENCY EXITS\nECONOMY\nCLASS\nCABIN\nGALLEY\nREAR\nENTRANCE\nLAVATORY\nPull exit handle inward and open.\nStep into exit.\nDO NOT REMOVE",
      "TO USE OXYGEN MASK\nOxygen mask will be automatically released.\nPull the nearest mask toward you.\nTO PUT ON LIFE VEST\nPull red strap and take vest out\nSlip it on over your head.\n* 1*SAFETY POSITION in the event that severe impact is expected\n60\nRemove glasses, shoes and all sharp objects.\nAdjust seat and fasten seat belt.\n= ⅝\nShould there be a loss of pressure, the oxygen masks will be automatically released to supply oxygen.\nPut the mask over your nose and inhale.\nYour life vest is located under your seat. Ask cabin attendants for children's vest.\nSnap the side rings and fasten securely.\nPull knobs downward for inflation.\non emergency landing or ditching, for your own protection, take the position shown below.\nGrasp ankles with both hands.\nIn case\nof pregnant women, or those carring an\ninfant,\nabove position is recommendable.\nPlease do not use FM radio and electronic computer in flight.\nNOT\nREMOVE",
      "SERVICE INFORMATION\nBABY\nKIT\n+\nJAL\nA variety of service is available; feel free to ask for your needs.\nLOCATION OF FACILITIES\n1)\nI Call button\n4 Table button\n2 Fresh air outlet\n5 Ash tray\n3 Reading light\n6 Table light\n12)\nWHAT'S IN THE LAVATORY\n2\nCosmetic set 2 Soap\n3 Towels\n4 Used towels 5 Call button\n6 Airsickness bagSanitary napkin\n8 Paper toilet seat cover 9 Toilet\npaper\n1 Paper cup Flush button (2 Tissue paper"
    ],
